Looking at the shape, the dot sits in the middle-left area. Working out the tiling: the P-shaped pentomino (piece D, rotated 90° counterclockwise) must occupy the cells forming the 2×3 block minus one corner around the dot — specifically the two cells above and the three cells in the dot's row. The remaining pieces (A, B, C, E) then fit exactly into the rest of the outline (the top-right hook, the left protrusions, and the bottom strip), confirming the placement.

The piece covering the dot is therefore D.

\boxed{D}
